1
00:00:00,386 --> 00:00:01,616
(Leonard:)Sheldon,

2
00:00:01,621 --> 00:00:03,551
(Amy:)I want you to take
that cap off.

3
00:00:03,556 --> 00:00:07,556
(Sheldon:)That nagging tone is
helping my anxiety, yeah.

4
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:09,930
(Sheldon:)But if you could maybe just go
ten percent less shrill,

5
00:00:09,929 --> 00:00:12,559
(Sheldon:)that'd really put the zip-a-dee
in my doo-dah.

6
00:00:12,565 --> 00:00:14,895
(Amy:)I'm sorry, but
you know we agreed

7
00:00:14,901 --> 00:00:16,771
(Amy:)not to bring work
to date night.

8
00:00:16,769 --> 00:00:19,099
(Sheldon:)There you go, perfect.

9
00:00:19,105 --> 00:00:21,105
(Amy:)Sheldon, stop it,
I'm not kidding.

10
00:00:21,107 --> 00:00:24,077
(Amy:)Take the cap off, and
put the notebook away.

11
00:00:24,077 --> 00:00:27,747
(Sheldon:)But after months of struggling,
I'm finally making progress.

12
00:00:27,747 --> 00:00:30,577
(Amy:)You don't need to drive yourself
crazy in order to be productive.

13
00:00:30,583 --> 00:00:32,583
(Sheldon:)Or do I, hmm?

14
00:00:32,585 --> 00:00:34,955
(Sheldon:)Sir Isaac Newton wrote
his Principia

15
00:00:34,954 --> 00:00:37,454
(Sheldon:)while convinced he was
an armadillo.

16
00:00:37,457 --> 00:00:38,957
(Amy:)That's not true.

17
00:00:38,958 --> 00:00:40,588
(Sheldon:)Yeah, well, maybe it is,
maybe it isn't.

18
00:00:40,593 --> 00:00:42,193
(Sheldon:)I have been
hallucinating lately.

19
00:00:44,797 --> 00:00:46,427
(Amy:)Sheldon, this has to stop.

20
00:00:46,432 --> 00:00:48,962
(Amy:)You need to get some sleep
and take care of yourself.

21
00:00:48,968 --> 00:00:51,768
(Sheldon:)Amy, I have gotten more done
in the last few days

22
00:00:51,771 --> 00:00:53,941
(Sheldon:)than I have since I made
the switch to dark matter.

23
00:00:53,940 --> 00:00:57,440
(Sheldon:)What if I stop doing this,
and it all goes away?

